From oehl at Psyres-Stuttgart.DE  Wed Jul  1 11:34:27 1998
From: oehl at Psyres-Stuttgart.DE (Jens Oehlschlaegel)
Date: Wed, 01 Jul 1998 13:34:27 +0200
Subject: Re: [S] copying and pasting blocks of commands
In-Reply-To: <3599F43C.2922A900@genedata.com>
References: <3599F43C.2922A900@genedata.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.3.96.980701133331.14771B-100000@sunserv>

options (prompt="; ", continue=";; ")

# looks like a nice trick
# but refrain from having a single command extended over several lines
# as e.g.
c("line 1"
, "line 2"
, "line 3"
)

# which looks like
; c("line 1"
;; , "line 2"
;; , "line 3"
;; )
[1] "line 1" "line 2" "line 3"

# cutting and pasting gives
; ; c("line 1"
NULL
; ;; ;; , "line 2"
Syntax error: ";" used illegally at this point:
c("line 1"
;
; ;; , "line 3"
NULL
; NULL
; Syntax error: "," used illegally at this point:
,
; ;; )
NULL
; NULL
; Syntax error: No opening parenthesis, before ")" at this point:
)

# Instead try 
options (prompt="\n ", continue="   ")

# then
c("line 1"
, "line 2"
, "line 3"
)

# looks like

 c("line 1"
   , "line 2"
   , "line 3"
   )
[1] "line 1" "line 2" "line 3"

 
# and cutting and pasting gives

  c("line 1"
      , "line 2"
      , "line 3"
      )
[1] "line 1" "line 2" "line 3"

But perhaps using the history function or even an editor is more helpful.
 
Best regards

Jens Oehlschlaegel-Akiyoshi

