From scw at io.harvard.edu  Mon Jul  6 19:10:44 1998
From: scw at io.harvard.edu (Steve Wofsy)
Date: Mon, 06 Jul 1998 15:10:44 -0400
Subject: Re: [S] prevention of releasing BATCH mode p
In-Reply-To: <B0000043784@mimesweeper.edfman.co.uk>
Message-ID: <199807061910.PAA05710@io.harvard.edu>

There is a simple solution to the question of a BATCH command replacement
that runs in the foreground.  All you need is an executable shell script
with one line,

(echo "invisible(options(echo=TRUE))"; cat $1)| Splus >$2 2>&1 

or if you want to keep the priority lower, 

 (echo "invisible(options(echo=TRUE))"; cat $1)| nohup Splus >$2 2>&1 

The command

yourscript infile outfile

does what you want.  

I thought this was in the FAQ.

scw

PS note if you don't what the command set to be in outfile, change
TRUE to FALSE
