From timh at statsci.com  Thu Jul  9 16:15:40 1998
From: timh at statsci.com (Tim Hesterberg)
Date: Thu, 09 Jul 1998 09:15:40 -0700
Subject: 
In-Reply-To: <19980709155301.27880.rocketmail@send1c.yahoomail.com>
References: <19980709155301.27880.rocketmail@send1c.yahoomail.com>
Message-ID: <199807091615.JAA26381@quake.statsci.com>

>Given a vector, I know how to find out its maximum value.
>How can I determine which element of the vector is that maximum  ?
>
>e.g  
>
>max(v) <- v[?]  

first.max <- function(x)
((1:length(x))[x == max(x)])[1]

first.min <- function(x)
((1:length(x))[x == min(x)])[1]

Also, for matrices:

mat.first.max <- function(x)
{
        i <- first.max(x)
        c(row(x)[i], col(x)[i])
}

mat.first.min <- function(x)
{
        i <- first.min(x)
        c(row(x)[i], col(x)[i])
}

Tim Hesterberg
