From fharrell at virginia.edu  Mon Jul 13 18:19:40 1998
From: fharrell at virginia.edu (Frank E Harrell Jr)
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 1998 14:19:40 -0400
Subject: [S] Summary: Object Browser and Starting S-PLUS 4.x
Message-ID: <003401bdae8a$cd202e00$5a6c8f80@fharrell.biostat.virginia.edu>

Thanks to Chuck Taylor and Duncan Mackay.  For advanced users,
Chuck Taylor (of MathSoft) has a .guiFirst function that streamlines
how the object browser is opened.  At present there is no way for a stored
object browser to contain other useful information such as
what the "Start in" field specifies (see below). 
For new users, Duncan Mackay (and I) feel that using a separate 
shortcut in each project directory is still the way to go.  Quoting from Duncan:

To start S-plus in the folder "C:\My Documents\MYSTATS\my Splus stuff", I
have the following line in the "Target" field of my Splus shortcut icon:-

"C:\Program Files\splus45\cmd\SPLUS.EXE"  S_DATA="C:\My Documents\MYSTATS\my
Splus stuff\_Data"  S_CWD="C:\My Documents\MYSTATS\my Splus stuff"

and the following line in the "Start in" field:-

"C:\My Documents\MYSTATS\my Splus stuff"

This does away with S-PLUS creating a separate _Prefs directory for
every project.

-Frank Harrell

