> Here is a possible solution: --> sweep
>
> > A <- array(1:12, dim=c(2,2,3))
> > w <- c(10,20,30)
> > B <- sweep(A, 3, w, FUN="*")
> > apply(B, c(1,2), FUN=sum)
>      [,1] [,2]
> [1,]  380  500
> [2,]  440  560

more efficiently,

d <- dim(A)
dim(A) <- c(prod(d[-3]),d[3])
B <- A %*% w
dim(B) <- d[-3]

The relies on the ordering of indices in an array; use aperm if
you needed to change them.

